From: selcarpa <selcarpa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-xiaomi-elish: adapt to kShimC RAM/framebuffer handoff

The kShimC runtime discovers the live splash scanout from the bootloader DT
and repopulates the Linux DT's /chosen simple-framebuffer template with real
address/size. Turn the fixed mainline framebuffer node into a disabled
template (no reg / no fixed geometry, no memory-region) and tag the splash
reservation with the runtime's expected "cont_splash_region" label so
kshim_dt_splash_reservation() finds it.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
@@ -39,13 +39,9 @@
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
 
-		framebuffer: framebuffer@9c000000 {
+		framebuffer: framebuffer {
 			compatible = "simple-framebuffer";
-			reg = <0x0 0x9c000000 0x0 0x2300000>;
-			width = <1600>;
-			height = <2560>;
-			stride = <(1600 * 4)>;
-			format = "a8r8g8b8";
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -208,6 +204,7 @@
 		cont_splash_mem: cont-splash@9c000000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x9c000000 0x0 0x2300000>;
 			no-map;
+			label = "cont_splash_region";
 		};
 
 		ramoops@b0000000 {
